chef -- talk like the Swedish Chef==================================    chefA stdin-to-stdout filter that rewrites English into the Swedish Chef's mockaccent, a letter and syllable at a time: `the' becomes `zee', `w' becomes`v', `o' becomes `oo', an `i' in a word becomes `ee' the first time, and soon -- and it barks "Bork Bork Bork!" at the end of every sentence.  Pipe anytext through it:    echo "The chef stirs the soup." | chef    chef < READMEJohn Hagerman, 1992, from the `silly' collection of dialect filters postedto Usenet.  It is a lex program; the scanner was generated here with thedisk's own flex from chef.l, which is in SRC/chef/ORIG.